# Build-context filter for .docker/Dockerfile.web (self-contained web
# frontend image). Per-Dockerfile ignore file, confirmed honoured by
# BuildKit for both `docker build -f` and `docker compose build` — see
# specs/017-hcloud-web-frontend/research.md section 8.
#
# Keeps only what the hcloud provisioning/configuration/destruction path
# and webui/ itself need: ansible.cfg, inventories/group_vars for
# all/hcloud/hcloud_linux/linux, playbooks/ minus the AWS/Windows/tart/
# docker-only task files and vars, roles/ minus the two Windows-only
# roles, scripts/, configuration/, webui/, requirements-web files.

# VCS and tooling metadata
.git
.gitignore
.github
.beads
.omc
.rtk
.agents
.codex
.specify
.claude
.devcontainer

# Documentation and specs (not needed to execute playbooks or serve the UI)
docs
specs
role-template
**/*.md
.markdownlint.json
.shellcheckrc

# roles/claude_code copies this .md as a data payload to desktop users'
# ~/Documents/Cline/ (tasks/configure.yml "Copy OMC setup prompt"), not
# documentation -- the blanket **/*.md exclusion above caught it too,
# breaking every configure run against a desktop-profile host with
# "Could not find or access 'setup-omc-prompt.md'".
!roles/claude_code/files/setup-omc-prompt.md

# Docker build files themselves. This Dockerfile is passed via -f and
# read directly by the client; it does not need to also be baked in via
# COPY. The runner image's own build files are unrelated to this image.
.docker/Dockerfile
.docker/Dockerfile.web
.docker/Dockerfile.web.dockerignore
.docker/entrypoint.sh
.docker/tests.yaml
.docker/tests-web.yaml
.docker/README.md

# Secrets — never baked into the image; host-mounted at runtime
**/vault.yml
.envrc

# Local state — lives in the host-mounted inventories directory
inventories/*_autogenerated.yml
inventories/*_known_hosts*

# VERSION is written at build time via the IMAGE_VERSION build arg;
# a stray host copy must not override it
VERSION

# Out-of-scope providers (spec.md Assumptions: hcloud only; tart and
# docker are local providers that cannot work from inside a container;
# aws needs a second credential model)
playbooks/tasks/create/aws.yml
playbooks/tasks/create/tart.yml
playbooks/tasks/create/docker.yml
playbooks/tasks/destroy/aws.yml
playbooks/tasks/destroy/tart.yml
playbooks/tasks/destroy/docker.yml
playbooks/vars/aws_defaults.yml
playbooks/vars/aws_linux_defaults.yml
playbooks/vars/aws_windows_defaults.yml
playbooks/vars/docker_credentials.yml
playbooks/vars/hostname_pool_aws.yml
playbooks/vars/hostname_pool_docker.yml
playbooks/vars/hostname_pool_tart.yml
playbooks/vars/tart_credentials.yml
inventories/group_vars/aws
inventories/group_vars/docker
inventories/group_vars/tart
inventories/group_vars/windows

# Windows roles and playbook. NOT excluded, despite being out of scope by
# profile: playbooks/configure-profile.yml has an unconditional (no
# `when:`) `import_playbook: ../setup-roles-windows.yml`, and
# `import_playbook` plus a play's `roles:` list are both resolved
# statically at parse time -- Ansible must find these files on disk before
# it can even start running configure-profile.yml against an hcloud host,
# regardless of whether the `hosts: windows` play inside ever matches
# anything. Dropping them breaks every configure run with "Unable to
# retrieve file contents ... setup-roles-windows.yml". The
# ansible.windows/community.windows/chocolatey.chocolatey collections stay
# dropped below: those are only needed if the play's tasks actually run,
# which never happens against a Linux-only hcloud inventory.

# Out of scope for this feature (spec.md Assumptions)
backup.yml
restore.yml
playbooks/backup
playbooks/restore
playbooks/update-versions

# Testing tooling: gated by the separate structure-test/pytest CI jobs
# that run against a checkout, not from inside the image
tests
requirements.txt
requirements.yml
requirements-web-dev.txt
pytest.ini

# Local artifacts and caches
container-structure-test-linux-arm64
lancedb
.venv
__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.DS_Store
